      "text": "a. (1) through (6) above in every subcontract or purchase order unless exempted by rules, regulations, or orders of the City Administrator issued pursuant to Executive Order No. 71 so that such provisions will be binding upon each subcontractor or vendor. The contractor will take such action with respect to any subcontract or purchase order as the contracting agency may direct as a means of enforcing such provisions, including sanctions for noncompliance; provided, however, that in the event the contractor becomes involved in, or is threatened with, litigation with a subcontractor or vendor as a result of such direction by the contracting agency, the contractor may request the City of New York to enter into such litigation to protect the interests of The City of New York.",
